Summary: Isn't It Time For Tru64 Unix Newsgroup ?

Currently Tru64/Digital Unix/OSF/1 articles are posted to a variety
of newsgroups:

  comp.sys.dec        Discussions about DEC computer systems.
  comp.unix.osf.misc  Various aspects of Open Software Foundation products.
  comp.unix.osf.osf1  The Open Software Foundation's OSF/1.

Assuming Compaq's marketing wizards aren't planning another name
change, isn't it time for Tru64 to have its own newsgroup ?

Someone from the OSF emailed me what the difference was between
comp.unix.osf.misc and comp.unix.osf.osf1. IIRC, comp.unix.osf.osf1
was to be used for Digital's OSF/1 and comp.unix.osf.misc for
OSF/1 products.

The following articles posted by David C Lawrence:

  o How to Create a New Usenet Newsgroup
  o How to Format and Submit a New Group Proposal
  o How to Write a Good Newsgroup Proposal

are posted regulary to these newsgroups:

  o news.announce.newgroups
  o news.groups
  o news.announce.newusers
  o news.admin.misc
  o news.answers

--Jerry Leslie     (my opinions are strictly my own)



