Steve Stoddard wrote:
> 
> I have an XP1000 with factory-installed Dig UNIX 4.0E with SRM set to
> autoboot the system.  Something bad happened and the boot hangs.  How
> can I stop the process and get into the SRM console (>>> prompt) 
<SNIP>
> saying that it can't find an NFS port.  If I let it go for a long time
> will it eventually give up and continue with the boot process?

If you are able to eventually get the sytstem to boot, do a "shutdown -h
now" to bring the system back to the ">>>". Once at SRM, you can "set
auto_action halt". Auto_action can be set for boot, halt, or restart.

It's times like this I'm glad my AlphaServer2000 has that little "halt"
button next to the power/reset switches.
-- 

Until soon...
