In article <37E03143.991AA1AE@midwest.net>, Steve Stoddard
<sstod@midwest.net> wrote:
>I have an XP1000 with factory-installed Dig UNIX 4.0E with SRM set to
>autoboot the system.  Something bad happened and the boot hangs.  How
>can I stop the process and get into the SRM console (>>> prompt) before
>it tries to boot the operating system?  I'm thinking that I can boot
>from CD-ROM, then stop it and enter single user mode and try to fix the
>problem.  The boot problem is that it cycles endlessly with a message
>saying that it can't find an NFS port.  If I let it go for a long time
>will it eventually give up and continue with the boot process?

As was mentioned, if you can actually get booted and logged in, then
use 

        shutdown -h now

If you can not reach that point, then during boot, keep hitting
Control/C until the system either stops in the console >>> or stops in
single user mode.



